ail\",\"$undefined\"]}]}]]}]]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b9:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"top-navigation__action-button\",\"data-display-for\":\"all-users\",\"data-donate-pending\":\"$undefined\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"none\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"aafp-btn\",\"href\":\"/afp/subscribe\",\"target\":\"_self\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"data-aafp-donate-trigger\":\"$undefined\",\"data-prevent-progress\":false,\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"aafp-btn__label\",\"children\":\"Subscribe\"}]}]}]\nba:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sec-nav\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"sec-nav-label\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"id\":\"sec-nav-label\",\"className\":\"sec-nav__label\",\"role\":\"heading\",\"aria-level\":3,\"children\":\"Related websites\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"sec-nav__list\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"sec-nav-item-0\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"target\":\"_self\",\"children\":[\"AAFP.org\",\"$undefined\"]}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"sec-nav-item-1\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/fpm\",\"target\":\"_self\",\"children\":[\"FPM Journal\",\"$undefined\"]}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"sec-nav-item-2\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/fpe\",\"target\":\"_self\",\"children\":[\"FP Esssentials\",\"$undefined\"]}]}]]}]]}]}]\nbb:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"hamburger-menu-modal__bg\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"bd:[\"$\",\"div\",\"6a6176a0f1d4\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0c4de3abfc86\",{\"children\":[\"Anatomic and physiologic changes of pregnancy influence the assessment, management, and prevention of trauma.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"tlrv5zqyvw9\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"tlrv5zqyvw9\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"3\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"9919c2ikpsv\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b6\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"6\"]}]]}],\" Physiologic changes include a 30% to 50% increase in blood volume and a 40% to 50% increase in respiratory rate.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"6g34f39w79e\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b7\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"6g34f39w79e\",{\"children\":[\"7\"]}]]}],\" Anatomic changes include elevated diaphragm, delayed gastric emptying, and progressive uterine growth. During the first trimester, the thick-walled uterus is well protected from trauma by the pelvic girdle. In the second trimester, relatively abundant amniotic fluid volume protects the fetus. By the third trimester, however, the now thin-walled and prominent uterus is exposed to blunt and penetrating abdominal trauma. The placenta is an inelastic organ attached to an elastic organ (the uterus). Placental abruption may occur when trauma involving acceleration and deceleration deforms the uterus and shears the placenta off its implantation site.\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"be:[\"$\",\"$L108\",\"7c1471f41c88\",{\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h2\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"086f9b9141a7\",{\"children\":[\"Assessment\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"pin\":\"assessment\",\"__private_owner-created-at__\":\"2026-03-27T21:12:31Z\",\"cta\":null}]\nbf:[\"$\",\"div\",\"c5548ae4cb46\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"11d3a8f34780\",{\"children\":[\"The most common pregnancy-related traumas are minor incidents, including motor vehicle crashes and mild blunt abdominal trauma. These situations require clinical judgment about the extent of maternal and fetal assessment. However, because insignificant trauma can result in fetal injury or demise, fetal monitoring recommendations for pregnant women with minor trauma are similar to those for women with major trauma.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"h81u45sbimr\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"h81u45sbimr\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b8\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"8\"]}],\"–\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"hd5d6r9vv7\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b10\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"10\"]}]]}],\" In patients who have experienced IPV, an assessment for depression and suicidality should accompany assessment for immediate safety.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"mk13upy067\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b11\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"mk13upy067\",{\"children\":[\"11\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\nc0:[\"$\",\"div\",\"4feb1b34ad06\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"e8bb3e8f70e2\",{\"children\":[\"In major trauma, the primary assessment should focus on airway, breathing, and circulation. Once the primary assessment has been completed, a secondary assessment should include obstetric and nonobstetric injuries and fetal well-being.\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"c1:[\"$\",\"div\",\"263bbf7335ba\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"3fbf7b5137bd\",{\"children\":[\"A placental abruption may become apparent shortly after the injury. Fetal monitoring in women who experience trauma at greater than 20 weeks' gestation should be initiated as soon as the patient is stabilized. The patient should be monitored by tocodynamometry for a minimum of four hours.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"soaihfv815\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"soaihfv815\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b8\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"8\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"objmqffckp\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"12\"]}]]}],\" Eight or more contractions per hour were present in the first four hours of monitoring in 100% of patients with an ultimate diagnosis of placental abruption.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"a3povteo0qo\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"a3povteo0qo\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b8\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"8\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"2we7hht6o2y\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b9\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"9\"]}]]}],\" If at least six contractions per hour are detected during the four-hour initial period, or the mechanism of injury presents a high degree of fetal risk,\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"fuhabxt0ne4\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b13\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"fuhabxt0ne4\",{\"children\":[\"13\"]}]]}],\" then 24 hours of monitoring is indicated.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"3yzx8hthbsk\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"3yzx8hthbsk\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"3\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"z3dss57orva\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"12\"]}]]}],\" Before viability (23 to 24 weeks' gestation), the fetal heart should be monitored via intermittent Doppler auscultation, and after viability, continuous fetal monitoring should be performed.\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"c2:[\"$\",\"div\",\"1567d2a1e337\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"56e5479e7add\",{\"children\":[\"Ultrasonography has poor sensitivity (24%) for detection of placental abruption. However, it is very specific (96%), resulting in a positive predictive value of 88% if abruption is seen and a negative predictive value of 53% if abruption is not seen.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"0nwbs7ycbcn\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b14\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"0nwbs7ycbcn\",{\"children\":[\"14\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\nc3:[\"$\",\"div\",\"e79e38bcfd1a\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"4e908b08084d\",{\"children\":[\"The Kleihauer-Betke test allows identification of fetal blood cells. It should be performed in pregnant women who sustain major trauma to detect fetomaternal transfusion, regardless of Rh status, to determine the degree of fetomaternal hemorrhage.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"zolw7r3to3q\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b8\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"zolw7r3to3q\",{\"children\":[\"8\"]}]]}],\" Although the Kleihauer-Betke test screens for the degree of trauma in all patients, the result is used only to dictate Rh immune globulin therapy in Rh-negative patients.\"]}]]}]}]\nc4:[\"$\",\"$L108\",\"f0314799ac38\",{\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h2\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0c28b0bfd8fe\",{\"children\":[\"Management\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"pin\":\"management\",\"__private_owner-created-at__\":\"2026-03-27T21:12:31Z\",\"cta\":null}]\nc5:[\"$\",\"div\",\"bbd6b7624897\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"360bd30cab54\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"jhicm88japm\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-f1\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"jhicm88japm\",{\"children\":[\"Figure 1\"]}]]}],\" provides an algorithmic approach to the management of trauma during pregnancy.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"tstjggznsue\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"tstjggznsue\",{\"children\":[\"3\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\nc6:[\"$\",\"$L9e\",\"b2f537ed3f05\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-f1\",\"numberText\":\"Figure 1.\",\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h3\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0c1cb008b0fa\",{\"children\":[\"Management of Trauma in Pregnancy\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"3e428f632fd0\",{\"children\":[\"Management of trauma in pregnancy. (bpm = beats per minute; FHR = fetal heart rate.)\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"c9c71bb29462\",{\"children\":[\"Adapted with permission from Mendez-Figueroa H, Dahlke JD, Vrees RA, Rouse DJ. Trauma in pregnancy: an updated systematic review. Am J Obstet Gynecol. 2013;209(1):6. http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/00029378.\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080135/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-f1-gif.gif\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":1946,\"height\":2074,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\"},\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"},\"isPrint\":\"$undefined\"}]\nc7:[\"$\",\"div\",\"dda91c591d7c\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"1032e68fff6d\",{\"children\":[\"MINOR TRAUMA\"]}]]}]}]\nc8:[\"$\",\"div\",\"b2174857c608\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"f233ef84cbaf\",{\"children\":[\"Management of minor trauma is limited to care of lacerations or fractures, discussion of appropriate analgesics, counseling about the signs and symptoms of abruption, and ensuring appropriate follow-up. Tetanus toxoid should be administered if tetanus toxoid, reduced diphtheria toxoid, and acellular pertussis (Tdap) vaccine has not already been administered during the current pregnancy. Appropriate referrals should be made to community-based advocacy groups for persons who have experienced IPV, and a plan should be made to ensure the safety of the patient and other vulnerable persons living in the household.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"g5beuxey7s\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b11\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"g5beuxey7s\",{\"children\":[\"11\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\nc9:[\"$\",\"div\",\"2d16751110ea\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"fe65e2431466\",{\"children\":[\"MAJOR TRAUMA\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ca:[\"$\",\"div\",\"199aaf5abbfc\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"06d81cf15eb1\",{\"children\":[\"When feasible, patients who have experienced major trauma should be transported to a hospital that has the resources to perform a timely trauma evaluation.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"fnvdvxtco2w\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"fnvdvxtco2w\",{\"children\":[\"3\"]}]]}],\" Because placental abruption has been reported to occur up to 24 hours following trauma, monitoring via tocodynamometry should be continued for a minimum of 24 hours if at least six uterine contractions have occurred or if there are nonreassuring fetal heart rate patterns, vaginal bleeding, significant uterine tenderness, serious maternal injury, or a positive Kleihauer-Betke test result.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"ji8zf0lgvjk\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"ji8zf0lgvjk\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"3\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"imd1zvqpa7s\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b13\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"13\"]}]]}],\" If none of these findings are present, the patient may be discharged home with precautions.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"hxiikfva2jj\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"hxiikfva2jj\",{\"children\":[\"3\"]}]]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"cj2dohhrurs\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-t1\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"cj2dohhrurs\",{\"children\":[\"Table 1\"]}]]}],\" provides evaluation and discharge criteria for blunt trauma in pregnancy.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"8i4axpbxj9n\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"8i4axpbxj9n\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b9\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"9\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"t1jk442fgq\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"12\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"109:T586,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ctable frame=\"hsides\" rules=\"groups\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eEvaluation\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003ePrimary maternal and fetal survey\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eLaboratory: blood type, Rh factor test, hematocrit measurement, Kleihauer-Betke test, coagulation studies\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eConsider obstetric ultrasonography\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eIf greater than 20 weeks' gestation, monitor for contractions\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eIf fewer than three contractions per hour, monitor for four hours, then discharge\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eIf three to seven contractions per hour, monitor for 24 hours, then discharge\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eDischarge criteria\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eResolution of contractions\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eReassuring fetal heart tracing\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eIntact membranes\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eNo vaginal bleeding\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eNo uterine tenderness\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eAll Rh-negative patients should receive Rh immune globulin therapy unless the injury is remote from the uterus (e.g., isolated distal extremity)\u003csup\u003e\u003ca href=\"#afp20141115p717-b12\"\u003e12\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e \u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"cb:[\"$\",\"$L9c\",\"df59b63fa15f\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-t1\",\"numberText\":\"Table 1.\",\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h3\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0591c1a68d43\",{\"children\":[\"Management of Blunt Trauma in Pregnancy\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"4f678b99860c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"pxxs9yp788\",{\"children\":[\"Information from references \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"dw9a2h2rhwa\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b9\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"9\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"3dex59a016j\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"12\"]}]]}],\".\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080153/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-t1-gif.gif\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":983,\"height\":1236,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"table\":\"$109\",\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\",\"showImageInline\":true},\"isPrint\":false,\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"}}]\ncc:[\"$\",\"div\",\"8a5bb538fb70\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"d7cc5a5b18ef\",{\"children\":[\"Between 24 and 34 weeks' gestation, if delivery appears imminent, 12 mg of betamethasone should be administered intramuscularly to promote fetal lung maturity, and repeated in 24 hours. All pregnant Rh-negative patients should receive Rh immune globulin therapy unless the injury is remote from the uterus (e.g., isolated distal extremity).\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"ols4t0p8q6s\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"ols4t0p8q6s\",{\"children\":[\"12\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\ncd:[\"$\",\"div\",\"6bf6dfc966e9\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"b0ebad3c8c2f\",{\"children\":[\"CARDIOPULMONARY RESUSCITATION\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ce:[\"$\",\"div\",\"77b2a0a035cf\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"fb8f47b2048b\",{\"children\":[\"Because of maternal physiologic changes, left lateral uterine displacement is required during cardiopulmonary resuscitation. This is performed by tilting the whole maternal body 25 to 30 degrees \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"wedna8nkunm\",{\"children\":[\"(\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"n3kvem54u4p\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-f2\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Figure 2\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"qhcfbwbjuof\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b15\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"qhcfbwbjuof\",{\"children\":[\"15\"]}]]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"jzl0dfyg199\",{\"children\":[\")\"]}],\", or by manual uterine displacement \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"jg585aqb61\",{\"children\":[\"(\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"bppt4t5mop\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-f3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Figure 3\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"6ccb5xcdavp\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b15\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"6ccb5xcdavp\",{\"children\":[\"15\"]}]]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"rdo5su9jit\",{\"children\":[\")\"]}],\". Manual uterine displacement may allow for more effective chest compressions because it avoids the need to facilitate a total body tilt.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"lcg29wzdoig\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b16\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"lcg29wzdoig\",{\"children\":[\"16\"]}]]}],\" All standard medications and defibrillation regimens may be used in advanced cardiac life support (ACLS).\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"xhy8tzxdkk\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b17\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"xhy8tzxdkk\",{\"children\":[\"17\"]}]]}],\" Unique aspects of ACLS include early intubation, removal of all uterine and fetal monitors, and performance of a perimortem cesarean delivery.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"4divtdjdyeq\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b18\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"4divtdjdyeq\",{\"children\":[\"18\"]}]]}],\" Modifications of resuscitative efforts in pregnancy are listed in \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"pol9cs3lvrp\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-ut2\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"pol9cs3lvrp\",{\"children\":[\"eTable A\"]}]]}],\".\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"cf:[\"$\",\"$L9e\",\"0165e6f06336\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-f2\",\"numberText\":\"Figure 2.\",\"heading\":null,\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"1858b59b65c1\",{\"children\":[\"Left lateral uterine displacement by tilting the pregnant woman 25 to 30 degrees.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"b4409687b9df\",{\"children\":[\"Reprinted with permission from Advanced Life Support in Obstetrics Provider Syllabus. Leawood, Kan.: American Academy of Family Physicians; 2010.\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080140/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-f2-jpg.jpg\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":983,\"height\":869,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\"},\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"},\"isPrint\":\"$undefined\"}]\nd0:[\"$\",\"$L9e\",\"739423164e17\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-f3\",\"numberText\":\"Figure 3.\",\"heading\":null,\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"e5478f0e2335\",{\"children\":[\"Manual uterine displacement.\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"9e9bde97940a\",{\"children\":[\"Reprinted with permission from Advanced Life Support in Obstetrics Provider Syllabus. Leawood, Kan.: American Academy of Family Physicians; 2010.\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080144/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-f3-jpg.jpg\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":984,\"height\":869,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\"},\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"},\"isPrint\":\"$undefined\"}]\n10a:Tc0b,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ctable frame=\"hsides\" rules=\"groups\"\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth align=\"left\" valign=\"bottom\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eAction\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth align=\"left\" valign=\"bottom\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eRationale\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eBasic life support\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"/\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003ePerform manual uterine displacement, or 25- to 30-degree left lateral tilt\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDecreased aortocaval compression\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eIncrease chest wall compression force\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDecreased chest wall compliance with breast hypertrophy and diaphragmatic elevation\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eUse cricoid pressure, if assistance is available\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDecreased gastric aspiration\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003ePerform compressions higher on the sternum (slightly above center of sternum)\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eElevated diaphragm and contents\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eRemove fetal and uterine monitors before defibrillation\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eLoss of adequate cardiac shock dose; produces skin burns at monitor sites\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eHeimlich maneuver; use chest thrust if unable to encircle the gravid abdomen\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eEnlarged uterus displaces diaphragm\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eAdvanced cardiac life support\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"/\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eStart intravenous therapy above diaphragm\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eAortocaval compression\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eEarly tracheal intubation; use short laryngoscope handle and smaller endotracheal tube\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDifficult ventilation with pharyngeal edema, breast hypertrophy, diaphragmatic elevation\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eConsider other etiologies (e.g., magnesium toxicity)\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eMagnesium used as tocolytic therapy\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eConsider left wide paddle, adhesive pad, or breast displacement\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDextrorotation of the heart; breast hypertrophy\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eVerify endotracheal tube with carbon dioxide detector\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eEsophageal detector more likely not to reinflate after compression\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eAlter ventilation volumes and rates\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eTailor ventilator support to oxygenation and ventilation\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003ePerform emergency hysterotomy after four minutes\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDecreased aortocaval and venous compression\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eContinue all maternal resuscitative efforts (cardiopulmonary resuscitation, positioning, defibrillation, and drugs) during and after cesarean delivery\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eDecreased aortocaval and venous compression\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d1:[\"$\",\"$L9c\",\"b615589173fb\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-ut2\",\"numberText\":\"$undefined\",\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h3\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"4556cd714b36\",{\"children\":[\"eTable A. Modifications of Resuscitative Efforts in Pregnancy\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"c6388bdd36b8\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"d3r9mnqhqoq\",{\"children\":[\"Information from:\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"f3ac10fc0e4f\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"phy33doluwh\",{\"children\":[\"Berg RA, Hemphill R, Abella BS, et al. Part 5: adult basic life support: 2010 American Heart Association guidelines for cardiopulmonary resuscitation and emergency cardiovascular care [published correction appears in\"]}],\" Circulation \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"17j8tsd7bu4\",{\"children\":[\". 2011;124(15):e402]\"]}],\". Circulation\",[\"$\",\"em\",\"vkjymvtlc5j\",{\"children\":[\". 2010;122(18 suppl 3):S685–S705\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"32def251acc8\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"xxxpyhqb9h\",{\"children\":[\"Jeejeebhoy FM, Zelop CM, Windrim R, Carvalho JC, Dorian P, Morrison LJ. Management of cardiac arrest in pregnancy: a systematic review\"]}],\". Resuscitation. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"8xrvn5pafxg\",{\"children\":[\"2011;82(7):801–809\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"83e3eb94203a\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"j50cjyr6umc\",{\"children\":[\"Sinz E, Navarro K; American Heart Association. Cardiac arrest associated with pregnancy. In\"]}],\": ACLS for Experienced Providers: Manual and Resource Text. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"etwem03xtcu\",{\"children\":[\"Dallas, Tex.: American Heart Association; 2013\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"99fd32a800c3\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"x3fg0cqiaam\",{\"children\":[\"Vanden Hoek TL, Morrison LJ, Shuster M, et al. Part 12: cardiac arrest in special situations: 2010 American Heart Association guidelines for car-diopulmonary resuscitation and emergency cardiovascular care [published corrections appear in\"]}],\" Circulation\",[\"$\",\"em\",\"rdovy0rtpzf\",{\"children\":[\". 2011;123(6):e239, and\"]}],\" Circulation \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"3w3cd9vzoy2\",{\"children\":[\". 2011;124(15):e405]\"]}],\". Circulation. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"i6z8svpgry\",{\"children\":[\"2010;122(18 suppl 3):S829–S861\"]}],\".\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080167/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-ut2-gif.gif\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":1951,\"height\":1867,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"table\":\"$10a\",\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\",\"showImageInline\":true},\"isPrint\":false,\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d2:[\"$\",\"div\",\"0e0153776d80\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"7d1ab37e23ce\",{\"children\":[\"PERIMORTEM CESAREAN DELIVERY\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d3:[\"$\",\"div\",\"0bd3d072bf82\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"eb007c50bd1d\",{\"children\":[\"Perimortem cesarean delivery may save the life of the fetus when performed after 23 to 24 weeks' gestation.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"r7dnlnzzhr\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"r7dnlnzzhr\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b19\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"19\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"1to9pp9r1l4\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b20\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"20\"]}]]}],\" Delivery increases venous return and cardiac output by 25% to 30%, may lead to a clear survival benefit for the mother, and has not been shown to be harmful.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"m4pbaukgc2s\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"m4pbaukgc2s\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b16\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"16\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"fb79rlg2rol\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b19\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"19\"]}],\"–\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"bccjswssjhr\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b22\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"22\"]}]]}],\" The American Heart Association recommends considering perimortem cesarean delivery if ACLS has not returned spontaneous circulation within four to five minutes of cardiac arrest.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"cdjqwmlm4re\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b18\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"cdjqwmlm4re\",{\"children\":[\"18\"]}]]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"yidtek23h3e\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"yidtek23h3e\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-t2\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Table 2\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"ht5alte3er\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-ut3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"eTable B\"]}]]}],\" describe considerations based on gestational age and issues related to perimortem cesarean delivery.\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"10b:T522,\u003ctable frame=\"hsides\" rules=\"groups\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eGestational age less than 20 weeks: emergency hysterotomy is not indicated for a single fetus, but it may be indicated for more than one fetus.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eGestational age 20 to 23 weeks: emergency hysterotomy is indicated to enable successful resuscitation but not for survival of the delivered fetus.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eGestational age greater than 23 weeks: emergency hysterotomy is indicated to save the life of both the mother and fetus.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003eEmergency hysterotomy should not be delayed while attempting to listen for fetal heart tones or to perform an ultrasonography to document gestational age. A uterine fundus measurement of 3 to 4 cm above the umbilicus correlates with a 23- to 24-week singleton gestation, and is a quick, easy assessment of gestational age that can be made in the field. Omission of an emergency hysterotomy, or delay in performing the procedure, may lead to the unnecessary loss of two lives, although the decision is multidimensional.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003ePersonnel with the appropriate skills and equipment should provide this service, in or out of the hospital.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003ed4:[\"$\",\"$L9c\",\"a3b7fb660e6c\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-t2\",\"numberText\":\"Table 2.\",\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h3\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"505db83746cd\",{\"children\":[\"Gestational Age in Emergency Hysterotomy\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":null,\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080156/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-t2-gif.gif\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":1076,\"height\":1166,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"table\":\"$10b\",\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\",\"showImageInline\":true},\"isPrint\":false,\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"}}]\n10c:T1569,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ctable frame=\"hsides\" rules=\"groups\"\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"bottom\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eFactors to consider\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth align=\"left\" valign=\"bottom\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eDiscussion\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eCardiac arrest\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"/\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the mother fails to respond to initial resuscitative efforts and the gestational age is greater than 20 weeks, personnel and equipment should be assembled for emergency hysterotomy. This will allow simultaneous continuation of resuscitative efforts and preparation for the cesarean delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIs the mother receiving appropriate basic life support and advanced cardiac life support care, including:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eCPR with compressions performed with the mother angled to the left?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEarly intubation with verification of proper placement of the endotracheal tube?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAdministration of indicated intravenous medications to a venous site above the diaphragm?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eHas the mother responded to arrest interventions?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre there any potentially reversible causes of arrest?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eSurvival probabilities for the mother and fetus decrease as the interval from maternal arrest increases.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhysicians should aim for an interval of five minutes or less from maternal arrest to delivery of the fetus. This goal requires efficient assembly of personnel and equipment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhysicians should not wait until five minutes of unsuccessful resuscitation have passed before beginning to consider the need to deliver the fetus emergently. The need for hysterotomy should be considered within minutes to enable assembly of personnel and equipment.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003ePhysicians should ensure that the mother has received superior resuscitative efforts. She cannot be declared “refractory” to CPR and advanced cardiac life support unless all interventions have been implemented and implemented well.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eMother-infant factors\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"/\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIs the fetus old enough to survive?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eHas too much time passed for the mother to survive?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIs the mother's cardiac arrest caused by a chronic hypoxic state?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhat is the status of the fetus at the time of the mother's cardiac arrest?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eRecognition of gestational age is critically important. Survival is unlikely for the infant born at a gestational age less than approximately 23 to 24 weeks and a birth weight less than 500 g (1 lb, 2 oz).\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eDo not lose sight of the goal of this dramatic event: a live, neurologically intact infant and mother.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe potential for reasonable outcome should be carefully considered before pushing the margins of survivability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEven if the fetus is unlikely to survive (gestational age of 20 to 23 weeks), the mother may benefit from emergency hysterotomy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eSetting and personnel\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"/\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre appropriate equipment and supplies available?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIs hysterotomy within the rescuer's skill “comfort zone”?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre skilled neonatal or pediatric support personnel available to care for the infant, especially if it is not full term?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eAre obstetric personnel immediately available to support the mother after delivery?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn both in-hospital and out-of-hospital settings, is there adequate staff and equipment support? In out-of-hospital settings, is bystander support available?\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEquipment should be regularly rechecked.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eEffective communication is key.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe whole team should have periodic drills.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eDifferential diagnosis\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"/\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eConsider whether persistent arrest is because of an immediately reversible problem (e.g., excess anesthesia, reaction to analgesia, severe bronchospasm). If it is, the problem should be corrected, and there may be no need for hysterotomy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eConsider whether persistent arrest is because of a fatal, untreatable problem (e.g., massive amniotic fluid embolism). If it is, an immediate hysterotomy may save the fetus.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd align=\"left\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cul data-list-type=\"simple-no-indent\"\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis also raises the problem of quickly reversible issues (improperly mixed medication [e.g., lidocaine, magnesium sulfate]).\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the cause is reversible or subacute, then timely management of problems may obviate the need for emergency hysterotomy.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d5:[\"$\",\"$L9c\",\"aec39ca3b6cd\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-ut3\",\"numberText\":\"$undefined\",\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h3\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"e115d5b8f0b3\",{\"children\":[\"eTable B. Perimortem Hysterotomy Issues\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"a09fc8ffd148\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"t4uaoxbuis\",{\"children\":[\"CPR = cardiopulmonary resuscitation\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"c046e9005fa4\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"2t6ff6r42od\",{\"children\":[\"Adapted from Advanced Life Support in Obstetrics Provider Syllabus. Leawood, Kan.: American Academy of Family Physicians; 2010\"]}],\".\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080170/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-ut3-gif.gif\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":1951,\"height\":2471,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"table\":\"$10c\",\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\",\"showImageInline\":true},\"isPrint\":false,\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"}}]\nd6:[\"$\",\"$L108\",\"18439cf34cea\",{\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h2\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"6b4e7253751b\",{\"children\":[\"Prevention\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"pin\":\"prevention\",\"__private_owner-created-at__\":\"2026-03-27T21:12:31Z\",\"cta\":null}]\nd7:[\"$\",\"div\",\"5797e122ceda\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"a1c6fa6688cb\",{\"children\":[\"MOTOR VEHICLE CRASHES\"]}]]}]}]\nd8:[\"$\",\"div\",\"833295a7e157\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"69c5fd1fbf6f\",{\"children\":[\"Overall, 2% of pregnant women are involved in a motor vehicle crash during their pregnancy,\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"sgc5tvovl8c\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b7\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"sgc5tvovl8c\",{\"children\":[\"7\"]}]]}],\" and an estimated 368 pregnant women per year die as a result.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"d4gq5tlclcu\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b23\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"d4gq5tlclcu\",{\"children\":[\"23\"]}]]}],\" Motor vehicle crashes account for more than 50% of all trauma during pregnancy, with 82% of fetal deaths occurring during these crashes.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"3kt6jdy5p05\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b24\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"3kt6jdy5p05\",{\"children\":[\"24\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d9:[\"$\",\"div\",\"2d111a15d276\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"1bc361cfd350\",{\"children\":[\"Seat belt use actually decreases during pregnancy, because women fear that the seat belt will hurt the fetus. In blunt trauma, the most common cause of fetal death is maternal death.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"8jexs15kslb\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b9\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"8jexs15kslb\",{\"children\":[\"9\"]}]]}],\" Incorrect seat belt use increases the risk of intrauterine injury and fetal death.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"kv89q2k11z\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b25\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"kv89q2k11z\",{\"children\":[\"25\"]}]]}],\" When women were properly restrained, adverse fetal outcomes occurred in 29% of motor vehicle crashes. In women who were improperly restrained, adverse fetal outcomes occurred in 50% of motor vehicle crashes.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"f65d9gf1qed\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b26\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"f65d9gf1qed\",{\"children\":[\"26\"]}]]}],\" Proper seat belt use should be a major prenatal counseling issue. The lap belt should be placed as low as possible under the protuberant portion of the abdomen and the shoulder belt positioned off to the side of the uterus, between the breasts and over the midportion of the clavicle \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"0fjdc9c5jbh\",{\"children\":[\"(\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"mthf63lnhy\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-f4\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Figure 4\"]}],\")\"]}],\". Placement of the lap belt over the dome of the uterus significantly increases pressure transmission to the uterus and has been associated with significant uterine and fetal injury. There should not be excessive slack in either belt, and both the lap and shoulder restraints should be applied as snugly as comfort will allow.\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"da:[\"$\",\"$L9e\",\"cc6658db3c7e\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-f4\",\"numberText\":\"Figure 4.\",\"heading\":null,\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"b588cb2bdce1\",{\"children\":[\"Correct way to wear a seat belt in pregnancy.\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080148/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-f4-jpg.jpg\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":1102,\"height\":1113,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\"},\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"},\"isPrint\":\"$undefined\"}]\ndb:[\"$\",\"div\",\"f6790f22fcb5\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"5bafbbefd5e6\",{\"children\":[\"Air bag deployment reduces injury to pregnant women and does not increase the risk of adverse pregnancy outcomes.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"4upeytoyi4d\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b27\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"4upeytoyi4d\",{\"children\":[\"27\"]}]]}],\" The American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG)\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"ywurqqrakuh\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b28\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"ywurqqrakuh\",{\"children\":[\"28\"]}]]}],\" and the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"56dqr0304f\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b29\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"56dqr0304f\",{\"children\":[\"29\"]}]]}],\" state that pregnant women who are occupants in motor vehicles should wear lap and shoulder seat belts and should not turn off air bags.\"]}]]}]}]\ndc:[\"$\",\"div\",\"46b86d9c644e\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",\"0790c741c926\",{\"children\":[\"INTIMATE PARTNER VIOLENCE\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"dd:[\"$\",\"div\",\"1daa8ac2396d\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"7f1719ff2344\",{\"children\":[\"Direct assault on the abdomen may occur in the setting of IPV. As a result, ACOG and the American Academy of Pediatrics recommend universal screening for IPV during pregnancy.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"wc2rht3az09\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"wc2rht3az09\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b30\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"30\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"im0uiaqajmq\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b31\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"31\"]}]]}],\" Likewise, the American Academy of Family Physicians states that all family physicians should be alert for physical and behavioral signs and symptoms associated with abuse or neglect.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"9hwb7ff8jxp\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b32\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"9hwb7ff8jxp\",{\"children\":[\"32\"]}]]}],\" The U.S. Preventive Services Task Force recommends that all women of childbearing age be screened for IPV.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"67h2rkbym9x\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b33\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"67h2rkbym9x\",{\"children\":[\"33\"]}]]}],\" A review of this topic was previously published in the May 15, 2011, issue of \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"gjyzfat6eyt\",{\"children\":[\"American Family Physician\"]}],\" (\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"cyqn0bfwv2\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"/afp/2011/0515/p1165\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"https://www.aafp.org/afp/2011/0515/p1165.html\"]}],\").\"]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"de:[\"$\",\"div\",\"dcbf7afe6b9b\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"b551f2921f0f\",{\"children\":[\"A patient who presents with a vague or inconsistent history of trauma should raise suspicion for battering.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"z9v01w7cpy\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"z9v01w7cpy\",{\"children\":[\"12\"]}]]}],\" Battering may escalate in pregnancy. The abdomen is the most common target for blows, kicks, and other assaults. \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"826kfww1bq4\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-t3\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"826kfww1bq4\",{\"children\":[\"Table 3\"]}]]}],\" lists other historical elements and signs that may indicate IPV.\",[\"$\",\"sup\",\"pirvrvpngqe\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"pirvrvpngqe\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"12\"]}],\",\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"cyexdofjmte\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b30\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"30\"]}]]}],\" Identified patients should be appropriately counseled and referred.\",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"4x8vk9yn7gc\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b30\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"sup\",\"4x8vk9yn7gc\",{\"children\":[\"30\"]}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"df:[\"$\",\"$L9c\",\"8c5afae754cd\",{\"pin\":\"afp20141115p717-t3\",\"numberText\":\"Table 3.\",\"heading\":{\"level\":\"h3\",\"text\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"2b974db8b1db\",{\"children\":[\"Possible Indicators of Intimate Partner Violence\"]}]]}],\"secondaryText\":null},\"subheading\":null,\"citation\":null,\"description\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"f3837a030ee9\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"em\",\"gdkobjzjl5k\",{\"children\":[\"Information from references \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"n0yry3ikjbn\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b12\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"12\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"$L89\",\"5fg0xnpkdxj\",{\"target\":\"$undefined\",\"href\":\"#afp20141115p717-b30\",\"aria-label\":\"$undefined\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"30\"]}]]}],\".\"]}]]}],\"image\":{\"src\":\"https://dgnvxbcc3-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1773080160/Journals/Automation/AFP/2014/1115/p717-t3-gif.gif\",\"alt\":\"\",\"width\":1076,\"height\":953,\"focalPoint\":\"middle_center\",\"aspectRatio\":\"auto\"},\"table\":\"\u003ctable frame=\\\"hsides\\\" rules=\\\"groups\\\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eDiminished self-image, depression, or suicide attempts\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eFrequent emergency department or physician's office visits\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eInjuries inconsistent with the stated history\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003ePartner insists on being present for interview and examination, and monopolizes discussion\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eProgressive isolation from support systems\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eReproductive coercion\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eSelf-abuse\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eSelf-blame for injuries\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eSymptoms suggestive of substance abuse\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd align=\\\"left\\\" valign=\\\"top\\\"\u003eUnwanted touching or fondling\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\",\"noRightsText\":\"$undefined\",\"displaySettings\":{\"hideEnlarge\":\"$undefined\",\"hidePrint\":\"$undefined\",\"hideDescription\":\"$undefined\",\"showImageInline\":true},\"isPrint\":false,\"nntRating\":\"$undefined\",\"i18n\":{\"enlarge\":\"Enlarge\",\"print\":\"Print\"}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"e0:[\"$\",\"div\",\"2729d6a11fef\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0418ab137536\",{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"footnote\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"0418ab137536\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0a5a7a96b93d\",{\"children\":[\"Data Sources\"]}],\": Drawing on the literature search completed in October 2013 for the American Academy of Family Physicians' Advanced Life Support in Obstetrics Chapter K: Maternal Resuscitation, we searched the Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews, the National Guideline Clearinghouse, and PubMed utilizing the key words trauma, motor vehicle crashes, pregnancy, abruption, and perimortem cesarean delivery, both individually and in combination. Search date: August 14, 2014.\"]}]]}]]}]}]\ne1:[\"$\",\"div\",\"cd0bfd683285\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"f6e8a19f040a\",{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"footnote\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"f6e8a19f040a\",{\"children\":[\"The opinions and assertions contained herein are the private views of the authors and are not to be construed as official or as reflecting the views of the U.S. Army, Navy, or Air Force Medical Departments or the U.S. Army, Navy, Air Force, or Public Health Service.\"]}]]}]]}]}]\ne2:[\"$\",\"div\",\"3286636cbd5b\",{\"className\":\"text-block mb-body-para body-copy has-rich-text container text-container\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"69441c55d0c5\",{\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"footnote\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"69441c55d0c5\",{\"children\":[\"This article is one in a series on “Advanced Life Support in Obstetrics (ALSO),” initially established by Mark Deutchman, MD, Denver, Colo. The series is now coordinated by Larry Leeman, MD, MPH, ALSO Managing Editor, Albuquerque, N.M.\"]}]]}]]}]}]\ne5:[\"$\",\"em\",\"wiyteuobc8\",{\"children\":[\"Am J Obstet Gynecol.\"]}]\ne6:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"25028eb0b2bb\",{\"children\":[\"Glantz C, Purnell L. Clinical utility of sonography in the diagnosis and treatment of placental abruption. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"l8n7nmnlej\",{\"children\":[\"J Ultrasound Med.\"]}],\" 2002;21(8):837-840.\"]}]]}]\ne7:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"69a1c4ea0e46\",{\"children\":[\"Advanced Life Support in Obstetrics Provider Syllabus. Leawood, Kan.: American Academy of Family Physicians; 2010.\"]}]]}]\ne8:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"rich-text\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"5729a3ff3cc5\",{\"children\":[\"Jeejeebhoy FM, Zelop CM, Windrim R, Carvalho JC, Dorian P, Morrison LJ. Management of cardiac arrest in pregnancy: a systematic review. \",[\"$\",\"em\",\"k2kiyv08rqf\",{\"children\":[\"Resuscitation.\"]}],\" 2011;82(7):801-809.\"]}]]}]\ne9: